memory management
*Memory management is the process of allocating (giving) and deallocating
 (freeing) memory while a Java program is running.
 *Java does this automatically using the JVM (Java Virtual Machine) and
  the Garbage Collector (GC).

                  JVM Memory
        +-----------------------+
        |       Heap            |  <-- Objects, Arrays
        +-----------------------+
        |       Stack           |  <-- Method calls, Local variables
        +-----------------------+
        | Method Area (Meta)    |  <-- Class      information, Static variables
        +-----------------------+
        | PC Register           |
        +-----------------------+
        | Native Method Stack   |
        +-----------------------+

1. Stack Memory
Stores local variables.
Stores method calls.
Each method gets its own stack frame.
Memory is automatically removed when the method finishes.
2. Heap Memory
Stores objects and arrays.
Shared by all threads.
Managed by the Garbage Collector.
the memory allowgation is not continues
